#20 37.27   --project-path <path>
#20 37.27                         Path to the project folder. Your project folder should
#20 37.27                         contain subfolders for each dataset. Each dataset
#20 37.27                         should have an "images" folder.
#20 37.27   --end-with <string>, -e <string>
#20 37.27                         End processing at this stage. Can be one of: dataset,
#20 37.27                         split, merge, opensfm, openmvs, odm_filterpoints,
#20 37.27                         odm_meshing, mvs_texturing, odm_georeferencing,
#20 37.27                         odm_dem, odm_orthophoto, odm_report, odm_postprocess.
#20 37.27                         Default: odm_postprocess
#20 37.27   --rerun <string>, -r <string>
#20 37.27                         Rerun this stage only and stop. Can be one of:
#20 37.27                         dataset, split, merge, opensfm, openmvs,
#20 37.27                         odm_filterpoints, odm_meshing, mvs_texturing,
#20 37.27                         odm_georeferencing, odm_dem, odm_orthophoto,
#20 37.27                         odm_report, odm_postprocess. Default: None
#20 37.27   --rerun-all           Permanently delete all previous results and rerun the
#20 37.27                         processing pipeline.
#20 37.27   --rerun-from <string>
#20 37.27                         Rerun processing from this stage. Can be one of:
#20 37.27                         dataset, split, merge, opensfm, openmvs,
#20 37.27                         odm_filterpoints, odm_meshing, mvs_texturing,
#20 37.27                         odm_georeferencing, odm_dem, odm_orthophoto,
#20 37.27                         odm_report, odm_postprocess. Default: None
#20 37.27   --min-num-features <integer>
#20 37.27                         Minimum number of features to extract per image. More
#20 37.27                         features can be useful for finding more matches
#20 37.27                         between images, potentially allowing the
#20 37.27                         reconstruction of areas with little overlap or
#20 37.27                         insufficient features. More features also slow down
#20 37.27                         processing. Default: 10000
#20 37.27   --feature-type <string>
#20 37.27                         Choose the algorithm for extracting keypoints and
#20 37.27                         computing descriptors. Can be one of: akaze, dspsift,
#20 37.27                         hahog, orb, sift. Default: dspsift
#20 37.27   --feature-quality <string>
#20 37.27                         Set feature extraction quality. Higher quality
#20 37.27                         generates better features, but requires more memory
#20 37.27                         and takes longer. Can be one of: ultra, high, medium,
#20 37.27                         low, lowest. Default: high
#20 37.27   --matcher-type <string>
#20 37.27                         Matcher algorithm, Fast Library for Approximate
#20 37.27                         Nearest Neighbors or Bag of Words. FLANN is slower,
#20 37.27                         but more stable. BOW is faster, but can sometimes miss
#20 37.27                         valid matches. BRUTEFORCE is very slow but robust.Can
#20 37.27                         be one of: bow, bruteforce, flann. Default: flann
#20 37.27   --matcher-neighbors <positive integer>
#20 37.27                         Perform image matching with the nearest images based
#20 37.27                         on GPS exif data. Set to 0 to match by triangulation.
#20 37.27                         Default: 0
#20 37.27   --matcher-order <positive integer>
#20 37.27                         Perform image matching with the nearest N images based
#20 37.27                         on image filename order. Can speed up processing of
#20 37.27                         sequential images, such as those extracted from video.
#20 37.27                         It is applied only on non-georeferenced datasets. Set
#20 37.27                         to 0 to disable. Default: 0
#20 37.27   --use-fixed-camera-params
#20 37.27                         Turn off camera parameter optimization during bundle
#20 37.27                         adjustment. This can be sometimes useful for improving
#20 37.27                         results that exhibit doming/bowling or when images are
#20 37.27                         taken with a rolling shutter camera. Default: False
#20 37.27   --cameras <json>      Use the camera parameters computed from another
#20 37.27                         dataset instead of calculating them. Can be specified
#20 37.27                         either as path to a cameras.json file or as a JSON
#20 37.27                         string representing the contents of a cameras.json
#20 37.27                         file. Default:
#20 37.27   --camera-lens <string>
#20 37.27                         Set a camera projection type. Manually setting a value
#20 37.27                         can help improve geometric undistortion. By default
#20 37.27                         the application tries to determine a lens type from
#20 37.27                         the images metadata. Can be one of: auto, perspective,
#20 37.27                         brown, fisheye, fisheye_opencv, spherical,
#20 37.27                         equirectangular, dual. Default: auto
#20 37.27   --radiometric-calibration <string>
#20 37.27                         Set the radiometric calibration to perform on images.
#20 37.27                         When processing multispectral and thermal images you
#20 37.27                         should set this option to obtain
#20 37.27                         reflectance/temperature values (otherwise you will get
#20 37.27                         digital number values). [camera] applies black level,
#20 37.27                         vignetting, row gradient gain/exposure compensation
#20 37.27                         (if appropriate EXIF tags are found) and computes
#20 37.27                         absolute temperature values. [camera+sun] is
#20 37.27                         experimental, applies all the corrections of [camera],
#20 37.27                         plus compensates for spectral radiance registered via
#20 37.27                         a downwelling light sensor (DLS) taking in
#20 37.27                         consideration the angle of the sun. Can be one of:
#20 37.27                         none, camera, camera+sun. Default: none
#20 37.27   --max-concurrency <positive integer>
#20 37.27                         The maximum number of processes to use in various
#20 37.27                         processes. Peak memory requirement is ~1GB per thread
#20 37.27                         and 2 megapixel image resolution. Default: 12
#20 37.27   --use-hybrid-bundle-adjustment
#20 37.27                         Run local bundle adjustment for every image added to
#20 37.27                         the reconstruction and a global adjustment every 100
#20 37.27                         images. Speeds up reconstruction for very large
#20 37.27                         datasets. Default: False
#20 37.27   --sfm-algorithm <string>
#20 37.27                         Choose the structure from motion algorithm. For aerial
#20 37.27                         datasets, if camera GPS positions and angles are
#20 37.27                         available, triangulation can generate better results.
#20 37.27                         For planar scenes captured at fixed altitude with
#20 37.27                         nadir-only images, planar can be much faster. Can be
#20 37.27                         one of: incremental, triangulation, planar. Default:
#20 37.27                         incremental
#20 37.27   --sfm-engine <string>
#20 37.27                         Choose the SfM backend engine. opensfm uses the
#20 37.27                         current default OpenSfM pipeline. colmap uses COLMAP
#20 37.27                         for sparse reconstruction with optional GPU
#20 37.27                         acceleration. Can be one of: opensfm, colmap. Default:
#20 37.27                         opensfm
#20 37.27   --sfm-no-partial      Do not attempt to merge partial reconstructions. This
#20 37.27                         can happen when images do not have sufficient overlap
#20 37.27                         or are isolated. Default: False
#20 37.27   --sky-removal         Automatically compute image masks using AI to remove
#20 37.27                         the sky. Experimental. Default: False
#20 37.27   --bg-removal          Automatically compute image masks using AI to remove
#20 37.27                         the background. Experimental. Default: False
#20 37.27   --use-3dmesh          Use a full 3D mesh to compute the orthophoto instead
#20 37.27                         of a 2.5D mesh. This option is a bit faster and
#20 37.27                         provides similar results in planar areas. Default:
#20 37.27                         False
#20 37.27   --skip-3dmodel        Skip generation of a full 3D model. This can save time
#20 37.27                         if you only need 2D results such as orthophotos and
#20 37.27                         DEMs. Default: False
#20 37.27   --skip-report         Skip generation of PDF report. This can save time if
#20 37.27                         you don't need a report. Default: False
#20 37.27   --skip-orthophoto     Skip generation of the orthophoto. This can save time
#20 37.27                         if you only need 3D results or DEMs. Default: False
#20 37.27   --ignore-gsd          Ignore Ground Sampling Distance (GSD).A memory and
#20 37.27                         processor hungry change relative to the default
#20 37.27                         behavior if set to true. Ordinarily, GSD estimates are
#20 37.27                         used to cap the maximum resolution of image outputs
#20 37.27                         and resizes images when necessary, resulting in faster
#20 37.27                         processing and lower memory usage. Since GSD is an
#20 37.27                         estimate, sometimes ignoring it can result in slightly
